{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]I was standin’ by the [A]road in Black Jack [Em]County.
Not knowing that the [D]Sheriff paid a [B]bounty,
For [Em]men like me who [D]didn’t have a [A]penny to their [B]name.
He [Em]locked my legs in [A]35 pounds
Of [Em]Black Jack [B]County [Em]chain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]All we had to [A]eat was bread and [Em]water,
Everyday we had to [D]build his road a [B]mile and a quarter,
A [Em]black snake whip would [D]sting our backs
If [A]some poor fool [B]complained,
But we [Em]couldn’t fight back wearing [A]35 pounds
Of [Em]Black Jack [B]County [Em]chain.
{end_of_verse}

