{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]Then one night while the [A]Sheriff lay a [Em]sleepin’,
We all gathered [D]round him, slowly [B]creepin’,
Heaven [Em]help me to [D]forget that night [A]in the cold cold [B]rain,
When we [Em]beat him to death with [A]35 pounds
Of [Em]Black Jack [B]County [Em]chain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Em]The wounds have all [A]healed and I am [Em]thankful,
And there’s nothing left but [D]scars around my [B]ankle.
But [Em]best of all no [D]man will ever [A]be a slave [B]again,
To a [Em]black snake whip and [A]35 pounds
Of [Em]Black Jack [B]County [Em]chain.
{end_of_verse}

